  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#jew_pizza_analogical_mapping",
  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "jew_pizza_analogical_mapping",
  "label": "Jew is mapped onto Pizza",
  "description": "The textual question 'what's the difference between a Jew and a pizza?' and the punchline 'a pizza doesn't scream when you put it in the oven' create an analogical mapping where the Jewish man (visual entity) is equated with a pizza (visual entity). This mapping is explicitly stated in the text and reinforced by the visual juxtaposition of the man and the pizza. The mapping is hateful and antisemitic, reducing the Jewish man to an inanimate object, specifically invoking the historical antisemitic trope of the 'Jew as screaming in the oven' during the Holocaust.",
